///1ASM
Help by Willem Aandewiel
ASM - Assemble 8080 source code

///2SYNTAX
ASM name
Reads name.ASM and creates name.HEX and name.PRN.
Omit the .ASM extension in this simple command form.

///2EXAMPLE
With DEMO.ASM on E: and ASM.COM on A:

  E>A:ASM DEMO
  E>TYPE DEMO.PRN
  E>A:LOAD DEMO
  E>DEMO

Run LOAD only after correcting all assembly errors.

///2FILES
.ASM is the source. .PRN lists source lines, addresses and errors.
.HEX contains Intel HEX data. LOAD converts it into a .COM file.
ASM is the basic 8080 assembler. For macros, use a tool such as MAC.

///2ERRORS
A generated HEX file does not prove that assembly was successful.
Inspect error letters beside source lines. Check labels and opcodes.
For ASM 2.0, use ASCII source with CRLF and unique short symbols.
USE FACTOR indicates symbol table usage, not the number of errors.
